Apple’s productivity and creativity apps ...\\n\\n5. [Kristin Huguet Quayle](https://www.apple.com/leadership/kristin-huguet-quayle/)\\nKristin is responsible for Apple’s global communications strategy, leading the public relations team as well as employee communications. Kristin joined Apple’s Communications team in 2005, and led the Corporate PR team for seven years, most recently as vice president. Throughout her tenure at Apple, Kristin has played an instrumental role ...\\n\\n6. [Katherine Adams](https://www.apple.com/leadership/katherine-adams/)\\nKatherine Adams is Apple’s general counsel and senior vice president of Legal and Global Security, reporting to CEO Tim Cook. Kate serves on the company’s executive team and oversees all legal matters, including corporate governance, intellectual property, litigation and securities compliance, global security, and privacy.\\n\\n7. [Luca Maestri](https://www.apple.com/leadership/luca-maestri/)\\nLuca joined Apple in 2013 as vice president of Finance and corporate controller, and has worked closely with Apple’s senior leadership since his arrival. Luca has over 25 years of experience building and leading finance teams in global companies with significant operating scale and complexity. Prior to joining Apple, Luca was CFO at Xerox and ...\\n\\n8. [Sabih Khan](https://www.apple.com/leadership/sabih-khan/)\\nSabih Khan is Apple’s senior vice president of Operations reporting to COO Jeff Williams. Sabih is in charge of Apple’s global supply chain, ensuring product quality and overseeing planning, procurement, manufacturing, logistics and product fulfillment functions, as well as Apple’s supplier responsibility programs that protect and educate workers at production facilities around the world.\\n\\n9. [Tor Myhren](https://www.apple.com/leadership/tor-myhren/)\\nTor Myhren is Apple’s vice president of Marketing Communications, reporting to CEO Tim Cook. Tor joined Apple in 2016 from Grey, where he was president and worldwide chief creative officer. As head of the Marketing Communications group, Tor leads a talented and creative team focused on Apple’s advertising, internet presence, package design ...\\n\\n10. [Johny Srouji](https://www.apple.com/leadership/johny-srouji/)\\nJohny Srouji serves as senior vice president of Hardware Technologies at Apple, reporting to CEO Tim Cook. Johny has built one of the world’s strongest and most innovative teams of silicon and technology engineers, leading breakthrough custom chips and hardware technologies, including Apple silicon, batteries, cameras, storage controllers, sensors, displays, and other critical technologies ...\\n\\n11. [Leadership and Governance](https://investor.apple.com/leadership-and-governance/default.aspx)\\nApple's Board of Directors oversees the Chief Executive Officer and other senior management in the competent and ethical operation of Apple on a day-to-day basis and assures that the long-term interests of shareholders are being served. To satisfy the Board's duties, directors are expected to take a proactive, focused approach to their ...\\n\\n12. [Leadership and Governance - Apple](https://investor.apple.com/leadership-and-governance/default.aspx)\\nApple's Board of Directors oversees the Chief Executive Officer and other senior management in the competent and ethical operation of Apple on a day-to-day basis and assures that the long-term interests of shareholders are being served. To satisfy the Board's duties, directors are expected to take a proactive, focused approach to their ...\\n\\n13. [Meet the Apple Board of Directors - AdvisoryCloud](https://advisorycloud.com/blog/meet-the-apple-board-of-directors)\\nThe members of the Apple Board of Directors. Tech giant Apple's Board of Directors consists of some of the most accomplished business executives and industry luminaries in the world. The current members of the Board are as follows: Tim Cook. Tim Cook is the current CEO of Apple, and he also serves as the Chairman of the Board.\\n\\n14. [APPLE INC Executive Salaries & Other Compensation - Salary.com](https://www1.salary.com/APPLE-INC-Executive-Salaries.html)\\nFor its 2023 fiscal year, APPLE INC, listed the following CEO pay ratio data on its annual proxy statement to the SEC. ... Tim Cook: CEO Pay $63,209,845: Median Employee Pay $94,118: CEO Pay Ratio 672:1: Board of Directors in APPLE INC. For its 2023 fiscal year, APPLE INC, listed the following board members on its annual proxy statement to the ...\\n\\n15. [Apple Inc.: Shareholders Board Members Managers and Company Profile ...](https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/APPLE-INC-4849/company/)\\n2023 2024; Americas 125B 153B 170B 163B 167B Europe 68.64B 89.31B 95.12B 94.29B 101B ... Members of the board: Apple Inc. Manager Title Age Since; Arthur Levinson ... Director/Board Member 69 2024-02-27 Composition of the Board of Directors ...\\n\\n16. [Al Gore exiting Apple's board of directors after hitting age limit](https://nypost.com/2024/01/12/business/al-gore-exiting-apples-board-of-directors-after-hitting-age-limit/)\\nAlso exiting from the eight-member board is former Boeing CFO James Bell, also 75, who had held a seat since 2015. Apple’s board has a longstanding policy that directors can’t stand for re ...\\n\\n17. [Apple Inc.: Governance, Directors and Executives & Committees ...](https://in.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/APPLE-INC-4849/company-governance/)\\nFind the composition of the Board of Directors of Apple Inc. (Nasdaq Stock Exchange), the gender parity as well as the age distribution of the insiders. ... 01/03/2023 Mike Fenger - Sales & Marketing ... Director/Board Member 01/01/1999 ...\\n\\n18. [AAPL | Apple Inc. Company Profile & Executives - WSJ](https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/AAPL/company-people)\\nBoard of Directors. Name/Title Current Board Membership; Timothy Donald Cook Chief Executive Officer & Director: Apple, Inc. Wanda M. Austin Director: Apple, Inc. Arthur D. Levinson Independent ...\\n\\n19. [Apple Inc.: Governance, Directors and Executives & Committees ...](https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/APPLE-INC-4849/company-governance/)\\nFind the composition of the Board of Directors of Apple Inc. (Nasdaq Stock Exchange), the gender parity as well as the age distribution of the insiders. ... Director/Board Member 1996-12-31 2014-07-16 Independent Dir/Board Member 1983-06-30 ...\\n\\n20. [Apple Inc.: Shareholders Board Members Managers and Company Profile ...](https://uk.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/APPLE-INC-4849/company/)\\nApple Inc.: Shareholders Board Members Managers and Company Profile ...\", 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'user'}}, {'step': 3, 'agent': 'Corporate_Governance_Expert', 'message': {'content': \"To start, let's gather detailed professional histories and biographies of the identified board members to determine who did not hold C-suite positions before joining Apple’s Board of Directors.\\n\\n## Apple's Board of Directors:\\n1. Alex Gorsky\\n2. Andrea Jung\\n3. Monica Lozano\\n4. Ronald D. Sugar\\n5. Susan L. Wagner\\n\\nI'll now provide a brief profile for each member, focusing on their professional histories before they joined Apple’s board.\\n\\n1. **Alex Gorsky**: \\n   - Former CEO and Chairman of Johnson & Johnson.\\n   - Held various senior leadership positions at Johnson & Johnson before becoming CEO.\\n\\n2. **Andrea Jung**:\\n   - Former CEO of Avon Products Inc.\\n   - Had a significant career at Avon Products, including serving as President and Chief Operating Officer before becoming CEO.\\n\\n3. **Monica Lozano**:\\n   - Former CEO of ImpreMedia, LLC, and La Opinión.\\n   - Held numerous leadership positions within the media industry.\\n\\n4. **Ronald D. Sugar**:\\n   - Former Chairman and CEO of Northrop Grumman Corporation.\\n   - Held various leadership roles at Litton Industries and TRW Inc. before joining Northrop Grumman.\\n\\n5. **Susan L. Wagner**:\\n   - Co-Founder and Director of BlackRock.\\n   - Held the position of Vice Chairman at BlackRock.\\n\\nBased on this preliminary information, it appears all listed members had held C-suite positions at their respective companies. However, for accurate verification, we should thoroughly investigate their professional histories. \\n\\nNext, I'll fetch detailed biographies and professional histories to ensure precision.\", 'name': 'Corporate_Governance_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 4, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Address: bing: Alex Gorsky biography professional history\\nTitle: Alex Gorsky biography professional history - Search\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 1.\\n=======================\\nA Bing search for \\'Alex Gorsky biography professional history\\' found 10 results:\\n\\n## Web Results\\n1. [Alex Gorsky - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_Gorsky)\\nGorsky\\'s grandparents immigrated to the United States from Russia and Croatia. Gorsky was the third of six children of Albert and Loretta (née Bartolac) Gorsky [4] in Kansas City, Kansas. [5] When he was 12, his family moved to Fremont, Michigan, [1] where his father, a Korean War veteran, took a job as a marketing executive for Gerber Foods. [1] In high school, Gorsky was captain of the ...\\n\\n2. [Alex Gorsky J&J, Bio, Wiki, Age, Wife, Family, Salary, & Net Worth](https://factsbuddy.com/alex-gorsky/)\\nAlex Gorsky Net Worth 2021. In 2021 as Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Johnson & Johnson, his net worth was $100 million. How Old Is Alex Gorsky. Alex is a 63-year-old who was born on May 24, 1960, in Kansas City, Kansas, in the United States. Alex celebrates his birthday on May 24, every year. Did Alex Gorsky Get Vaccine\\n\\n3. [Alex Gorsky Biography](https://hbanet.org/sites/default/files/Documents/Events/Bios/JNJ%20Alex%20Gorsky%20short%20bio%20-%20updated%20October%202019.pdf)\\nAlex Gorsky is Chairman of the Board and Chief Executive Officer of Johnson & Johnson, one of just seven leaders who have served in the dual role since the company was listed on the New York Stock Exchange in 1944. Alex began his Johnson & Johnson career as a sales representative with Janssen Pharmaceutica in 1988.\\n\\n4. [Alex Gorsky Height, Weight, Religion, Net Worth, Age, Biography](https://thefamouspersonalities.com/profile/business-men-alex-gorsky)\\nAbout (Profile/Biography): Alex Gorsky was born on 1960, in Kansas City, Missouri, United States. Alex Gorsky raised in military family. Alex Gorsky enrolled for the United States Military Academy at West Point.Alex Gorsky graduated with a Bachelor of Science degree in 1982. After graduating from West Point, Alex Gorsky served in the U.S. Army ...\\n\\n5. [Alex Gorsky - Robert F. Kennedy Human Rights](https://rfkhumanrights.org/person/alex-gorsky/)\\nAlex Gorsky is Chairman of the Board and Chief Executive Officer of Johnson & Johnson and Chairman of the Executive Committee, the Company’s senior leadership team. Alex is the seventh person to serve as Chairman and CEO of Johnson & Johnson since it became a publicly traded company in 1944. Alex began his Johnson & […]\\n\\n6. [Biography of Alex Gorsky : The Wharton Global Alumni Forum-Zürich](http://www.whartonzurich07.com/bio-s-gorsky.html)\\nGorsky began his pharmaceutical career as a sales representative and held various roles of increasing responsibility in sales, marketing and general management. Mr. Gorsky holds a 1982 bachelor\\'s of science degree from the U.S. Military Academy in West Point, N.Y., and spent six years in the U.S. Army, finishing his career with the rank of Captain.\\n\\n7. [Alex Gorsky - George W. Bush Presidential Center](https://www.bushcenter.org/people/alex-gorsky)\\nAlex Gorsky is the Former Chairman & CEO of Johnson & Johnson, and one of just seven leaders to have served in the dual role of Chairman and Chief Executive Officer since the company was listed on the New York Stock Exchange in 1944. Alex began his Johnson & Johnson career as a sales representative with Janssen Pharmaceutica in 1988.\\n\\n8. [Alex Gorsky (born 1960), pharmaceutical executive | World Biographical ...](https://prabook.com/web/alex.gorsky/1445186)\\nAlex Gorsky, pharmaceutical executive. Named Honorable Mentor, Healthcare Businesswomen\\'s Association, 2009. Member Doylestown Hospital Board; Member of Philadelphia College Pharmacy, National Alliance on Aging, National Alliance for the Mentally Ill.\\n\\n9. [Alex Gorsky | Travis Manion Foundation](https://www.travismanion.org/about-us/tmf-staff-and-board/board-of-directors/alex-gorsky/)\\nFormer Chairman & CEO, Johnson & Johnson. Alex Gorsky is the former Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Johnson & Johnson. He began his Johnson & Johnson career with Janssen Pharmaceutica in 1988, advancing through positions of increasing responsibility in sales, marketing, and management until, in 2012, he became the seventh leader to serve in the dual role of Chairman and CEO. He became ...\\n\\n10. [Alex Gorsky - JPMorgan Chase & Co.](https://www.jpmorganchase.com/about/leadership/alex-gorsky)\\nAlex Gorsky retired from the Chairman and Chief Executive Officer roles at Johnson & Johnson in 2021 and then served as Executive Chairman during 2022. Mr. Gorsky currently sits on the boards of Apple, IBM and the Travis Manion Foundation, and serves on the Business Council and the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania Board of Advisors.\\n\\nAddress: bing: Andrea Jung biography professional history\\nTitle: Andrea Jung biography professional history - Search\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 1.\\n=======================\\nA Bing search for \\'Andrea Jung biography professional history\\' found 10 results:\\n\\n## Web Results\\n1. [Andrea Jung - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrea_Jung)\\nAndrea Jung (Chinese: 鍾彬嫻; pinyin: Zhōng Bīnxián; Jyutping: zung1 ban1 haa4; born September 18, 1958 [1]) is a Canadian-American executive, non-profit leader, and prominent women\\'s-issues supporter based in New York City.In April 2014, she became president and CEO of Grameen America, a nonprofit microfinance organization founded by Nobel Peace Prize winner, Muhammad Yunus. [2]\\n\\n2. [Andrea Jung Biography - life, family, children, parents, story, history ...](https://www.notablebiographies.com/supp/Supplement-Fl-Ka/Jung-Andrea.html)\\nAndrea Jung Biography ; Andrea Jung Biography. Andrea Jung (born 1959) went from being a lackluster student to attending the Ivy League\\'s Prince- ton University, and went on to become the CEO of Avon Products. ... Since becoming CEO of Avon, Jung has become known for her professional, businesslike demeanor and for her innovative ideas. Rarely ...\\n\\n3. [Andrea Jung Grameen, Bio, Age, Husband, Apple, and Net Worth - Facts Buddy](https://factsbuddy.com/andrea-jung/)\\nAndrea Jung Bio | Wiki. Andrea Jung is a popular Canadian-American executive, non-profit leader, and famous women’s-issues supporter based in New York City. Currently, Andrea works as the president and CEO of Grameen America, a nonprofit microfinance organization created by Nobel Peace Prize winner, Muhammad Yunus. She is also on Apple’s ...\\n\\n4. [Andrea Jung Biography - Infoplease](https://www.infoplease.com/biographies/society-culture/andrea-jung)\\nAndrea Jungbusiness executiveBorn: 1959 Birthplace: Toronto, Canada The oldest child of Chinese immigrants, Jung grew up speaking both English and Mandarin Chinese. Jung received a BA in English literature from Princeton University in 1979. After graduation, Jung joined the management trainee program at Bloomingdale\\'s.\\n\\n5. [Andrea Jung | Avon CEO, Philanthropist & Trailblazer | Britannica Money](https://www.britannica.com/money/Andrea-Jung)\\nAndrea Jung (born 1959, Toronto, Ontario, Canada) is a Canadian-born American businesswoman who was chairman (2001–12) and CEO (1999–2012) of Avon Products, Inc. She later became president and CEO (2014– ) of Grameen America.. Jung moved with her family from Toronto to Wellesley, Massachusetts, when she was a young child.Her father was an architect, and her mother was a chemical engineer ...\\n\\n6. [Andrea Jung - Wikiwand](https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Andrea_Jung)\\nAndrea Jung (Chinese: 鍾彬嫻; pinyin: Zhōng Bīnxián; Jyutping: zung1 ban1 haa4; born September 18, 1958 [1]) is a Canadian-American executive, non-profit leader, and prominent women\\'s-issues supporter based in New York City.In April 2014, she became president and CEO of Grameen America, a nonprofit microfinance organization founded by Nobel Peace Prize winner, Muhammad Yunus. [2]\\n\\n7. [Andrea Jung | Encyclopedia.com](https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/social-sciences-and-law/business-leaders/andrea-jung)\\nAndrea Jung [1]1959– Chairman and chief executive officer, Avon Products Nationality: American. Born: 1959, in Toronto [2], Ontario [3], Canada [4]. ... Jung has become known for her professional, businesslike demeanor and for her innovative ideas. Rarely personal in interviews, she once admitted to a reporter that she kept in her desk a ...\\n\\n8. [Andrea Jung 1959— Biography - Destined for success](https://www.referenceforbusiness.com/biography/F-L/Jung-Andrea-1959.html)\\nAndrea Jung 1959— Biography; Andrea Jung 1959– Chairman and chief executive officer, Avon Products Nationality: American. Born: 1959, in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. Education: Princeton University, BA, 1979. Family: Daughter of Hong Kong–born father (architect) and Shanghai-born mother (pianist and chemical engineer); married Michael Gould ...\\n\\n9. [Andrea Jung - CEO, Avon Products (1999-2012) - Life Stories](https://www.lifestories.org/interviewees/andrea-jung)\\nShe became the first female CEO in Avon\\'s history in 1999, and became chairwoman of Avon in 2001 until 2012. In April 2014, she became president and CEO of Grameen America, a nonprofit microfinance organization founded by Nobel Peace Prize winner, Muhammad Yunus. Jung has two children: Lauren from her first marriage, and James from her second.\\n\\n10. [Andrea Jung biography. President and CEO of Avon Products Inc.](https://biographs.org/andrea-jung)\\nThe Biography of Andrea Jung Andrea Jung is the president and CEO of Avon Products Inc., one of the most prominent companies in the beauty and skincare industry. She was appointed as the CEO of Avon in November 1999 and had been a member of the board of directors since January 1998. Jung first joined Avon in January 1994 as the president of the product marketing group in the United States.\\n\\nAddress: bing: Monica Lozano biography professional history\\nTitle: Monica Lozano biography professional history - Search\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 1.\\n=======================\\nA Bing search for \\'Monica Lozano biography professional history\\' found 10 results:\\n\\n## Web Results\\n1. [Monica C. Lozano - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monica_C._Lozano)\\nMonica Cecilia Lozano (born July 21, 1956) is the president of the College Futures Foundation, based in San Francisco. [1] Previously she was an American newspaper editor, the publisher and CEO of La Opinión [2] and CEO of its parent company, ImpreMedia, LLC. [3] Based in Los Angeles, La Opinión is the largest Spanish publication in the United States. [4]\\n\\n2. [Monica Lozano Biography - Infoplease](https://www.infoplease.com/biographies/art-entertainment/monica-lozano)\\nMonica Lozanonewspaper publisher Lozano studied political science at the University of Oregon and holds an honorary degree from Occidental College. Lozano is the president and chief operating officer of La Opinión, the largest Spanish-language daily newspaper in the U.S., which was founded by her family.\\n\\n3. [Monica Lozano - Leadership California](https://leadershipcalifornia.org/page/MonicaLozano)\\nLozano also advises women leaders to build teams, drive collaboration, and develop talent. “Always strive to find the best person for the role who will contribute excellence,” she says. Following her passion with purpose in a professional way has allowed her to do just that.\\n\\n4. [Monica C. Lozano - Wikiwand](https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Monica_C._Lozano)\\nMonica Cecilia Lozano (born July 21, 1956) is the president of the College Futures Foundation, based in San Francisco. [1] Previously she was an American newspaper editor, the publisher and CEO of La Opinión [2] and CEO of its parent company, ImpreMedia, LLC. [3] Based in Los Angeles, La Opinión is the largest Spanish publication in the United States. [4]\\n\\n5. [Monica C. Lozano - The Aspen Institute](https://www.aspeninstitute.org/people/monica-lozano/)\\nMonica C. Lozano is President and Chief Executive Officer of College Futures Foundation, a California-based private foundation. College Futures Foundation partners with organizations and leaders across the state to catalyze systemic change, increase college degree completion, and close equity gaps so that educational opportunity becomes a reality for every student, regardless of skin color ...\\n\\n6. [Monica Cecilia Lozano - American Academy of Arts & Sciences](https://www.amacad.org/person/monica-cecilia-lozano)\\nMonica Lozano has a thirty year record of accomplishment leading diversified media organizations beginning in 1985 with the country’s leading Spanish-language daily newspaper La Opinión .She rose to become publisher in 2004 and in 2010 was named CEO of ImpreMedia. She led the transformation of ImpreMedia from a newspaper business to a multi-media, multi-platform, content company known for ...\\n\\n7. [Monica Lozano - LatinoJusticePRLDEF](https://www.latinojustice.org/en/monica-lozano)\\nLozano has committed much of her time to non-profit organizations including the National Council of La Raza where she served as board chair. In 2013 she completed a 12 year term as Regent of the University of California but was asked to return by Governor Jerry Brown who re-appointed Lozano in 2014.\\n\\n8. [Monica C. Lozano | CSU 